(Coverage: symlink with variable (non-literal) arguments in both
 positions. Also guards the codegen argument-parking scheme: each
 syscall argument is evaluated and parked on the stack before the next
 is generated, so future richer expressions in later positions can
 never clobber earlier ones.)

a text called linktarget is '/tmp/vox_test_symlink_vararg'.
a text called linkname is "/tmp/vox_test_link_vararg".

Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_link_vararg".
Remove the directory called '/tmp/vox_test_symlink_vararg'.

Create a directory called '/tmp/vox_test_symlink_vararg'.
Create symbolic link from linktarget to linkname.
On error print "symlink failed", exit 1.
Print "symlink succeeded".

Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_link_vararg".
Remove the directory called '/tmp/vox_test_symlink_vararg'.
